# XBD <iconv.h>
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Semantic content of <iconv.h> beyond the names the Tier 0 header check
# covers: the types and declarations the page gives, checked at build time.
# The header mutants for these arrive with the Tier 0 generator, so each
# says why it has no mutant yet.

assertion  XBD.iconv.h.001
anchor     basedefs/iconv.h.html#DESCRIPTION/iconv_t
anchor     basedefs/iconv.h.html#DESCRIPTION/size_t
class      required
says       <iconv.h> alone defines iconv_t as a type of which an object can
           be declared, and size_t as an unsigned integer type.
note       The page defers to <sys/types.h> for size_t.
test       t/001-types.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.iconv.h.002
anchor     basedefs/iconv.h.html#DESCRIPTION/iconv
anchor     basedefs/iconv.h.html#DESCRIPTION/iconv_open
class      required
says       <iconv.h> declares iconv(), iconv_close() and iconv_open() with
           the prototypes the page gives (a function without a prototype, or
           with other parameter or result types, does not match).
test       t/002-functions.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants
